A||||8||JohnnyK||Cheap performance||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-16-2000||11:27 PM||||Anyone know what good performance upgrades you can do to the Iron Duke with a limited amount of cash.. we'll say 200-300? I know someone is going to say K&N air filter..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But does anyone know how much horsepower the mods actually give? Thats sort of important to me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-16-2000||11:38 PM||||I believe you can still get a hooker header though summit.... Not sure about hp gain.  I'm guess in the vicinity of 5-10....  Also check out the holley tbi5 unit summit sells.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||04-16-2000||11:38 PM||||I believe you can still get a hooker header though summit.... Not sure about hp gain.  I'm guess in the vicinity of 5-10....  Also check out the holley tbi unit summit sells.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fotofrank||04-17-2000||01:36 PM||||If possible, port match the intake manafold to the head and exhaust manifold to head. You get some gain depending on engin. Install a MSD ignition and coil, with this combination ONLY use STEEL (no platinum)Plugs. The Holley 500-1 TBI also helps. If you can find a Holley intake manafold(out of production) The combination of TBI and intake works best.Also a free flow CAT and muffler can aid the the overall preformance. ||||reg||3
Z||000004||88formula||04-17-2000||08:30 PM||||Just forget about that engine and save your cash man, the Duck will never fly. It is not meant to and never will unless you spend a lot of cash.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||04-18-2000||01:48 PM||||I heard you could get big camshafts that would really boost power? Possible? Cheap (cheap enough).. ?||||reg||1
Z||000006||fotofrank||04-18-2000||02:51 PM||||The 2.5l is good for about 140 to 150 HP. that is with a stock block and crank.If you want a lot more go to a V*. If you like a challeng stick with the 2.5L. People will lol but self satisfaction is worth something too.||||reg||8
Z||000007||Cooter||04-18-2000||11:14 PM||||I have a MSD 6AL and matched GM style Blaster coil, GT muffler and Bosche +4 plugs on my 4cyl SE. It is not a powerhouse, but on the last tank of gas it got well over 30 MPG and has "decent" power. I gave up on any other modifications because they are cost prohibitive.||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||04-19-2000||02:27 AM||||The Hooker Tri-Y is probably the best thing you can do to uncork the Duke. I had an 87 4 cyl and did the K&N and replaced the air box (right behind the intake vent) out and replaced it with a pipe. I think that 140 is high even if you did the heads but I loved being able to keep up with stock V6 on our club trips and only having to top off the tank while they had to fill up the thirsty V6! I didn't try to get more power I was only trying to improve efficiency. And if I got 3/10 of a second and 2 miles faster on the 1/4 mile than I was happy with that too...||||reg||6
